Q: Codeigniter join two tables in model A: <pre><code>$this-&gt;db-&gt;select('*'); 
$this-&gt;db-&gt;from('user_registration');
$this-&gt;db-&gt;join('info', 'info.User_Id = user_registration.User_Id','left outer');
</code></pre>

Q: SELECT rows WHERE id NOT IN subquery with CodeIgniter&#39;s query builder A: <p>The problem lies in your model. You are not returning the proper array results. You have to first use <code>get()</code> to build the query and place it into a variable like <code>$q</code>, then use that variable with a the <code>result()</code> method to obtain the results, like this : </p>

<pre><code>$q = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get(); 
return $q-&gt;result();
</code></pre>
